    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d888">

                <pb facs="0707" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13007.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. R. Zubáran Capmany to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Confidential Agency of the Constitutionalist
                                Government of Mexico</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 25, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The undersigned, Confidential Agent of the Chief of the Constitutional Army of
                    Mexico, Don Venustiano Carranza, in compliance with special instructions, has
                    the honor of informing the Government of the United States, through the very
                    dign conduct of the Honorable Secretary of State, that on the twenty-second day
                    of August of this year, Mr. Carranza took charge of the Executive Power of the
                    Mexican Republic in accordance with the Plan of Guadalupe of March twenty-six,
                    nineteen hundred and thirteen.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Zubáran Capmany</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
